      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is unsafe. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg per day. The maximum daily dose for immediate-release metformin is generally 2,550 mg, and 1,700 mg is not a standard tablet strength (500, 850, and 1,000 mg are common). Entering this could cause serious harm, including lactic acidosis.\n\nPlease check the intended dose with the prescribing physician. Possible explanations include a transcription error or a confusion with another unit or drug. Once a licensed prescriber confirms the dose, they can enter the order or ask me to enter a corrected one. I'd want that confirmation from the prescriber, not only from a non-clinical request, before I place a medication order."
      }
